Z||000000||bHooper||09-20-2000||10:33 PM||||ive driven my car everyday this week... no problems (even on the racetrack at VIR).<P>tonight i get in to go out, and the right headlight goes up on its on (when the switch is turned on)... it hasnt done this in 4+ years!<P>the real problem was the serpentine belt.  on the way home, i noticed the volts were down... stopped @ micky D's, checked the belt... yep, it's started fraying and is lose.<P>i just put this one on a week ago!... that's 3 in 5 month's!!<P>fortunately, it didnt bust until i got 2 blocks from my house.  the car heated up a bit, spilling coolant in the driveway.<P>any hints/tips/thoughts on what im doing wrong with these darned belts?  couild there be a hidden problem, such as a bad pully, that i dont see?<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||8
